  "decision_summary": [
    "Promote the exact-M32 NVFP4 gate/up [17408,5120] single-slot raw-weight cp.async specialization. It preserves the existing K64/LD72 dual-resident-A, K256 scale-window, table-free-E2M1 computation and changes only how each K64 packed-weight stage reaches registers.",
    "Across five independent fixed-clock processes, the isolated two-distribution aggregate speedup is 1.07986x to 1.08897x with median 1.08128x; the existing dual-stream gate/up pair aggregate is 1.07323x to 1.16135x with median 1.12402x. All 40 isolated rounds and all 40 pair rounds are positive.",
    "Unprofiled production binaries improve the P33 prefix bracket by 6.315 ms, or 1.022810x, and two independent P513 B-C-C-B groups improve their prefix brackets by 1.022640x and 1.038431x. Every run generates token ID 9419 and text Hello.",
    "Matched P513/C32/max1 Nsys B-C-B reduces the exact gate/up marginal critical path from a 1,387.450576 ms baseline bracket mean to 1,261.214976 ms, or 1.100090x, and reduces prefix kernel union by 123.219520 ms, or 1.026968x. The source- and selector-unchanged exact-M32 down group differs by 0.0140% in this bracket.",
    "This is one 4 KiB shared raw-weight slot inside each kernel CTA, with the consumed uint4 held in registers before the next transfer starts. It is not a system-level double or triple buffer and does not alter the gate/up dual-stream scheduler, Prefill/Decode separation, request scheduling, or Decode."
  ],
